WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.940
Welcome to Causal Analysis and Resolution. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Identify why selected results occur and prevent unwanted recurrence.

2
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:20.590
Consider this scenario. Recurring defects keep returning after releases. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:30.960
Start with two steps: Select a recurring outcome. Then Gather facts and validate root causes. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:41.310
Continue with Implement a measurable preventive action. Then Review recurrence trends and effectiveness. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:41.310 --> 00:01:02.040
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous cause analysis records, action log, trend chart tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: treating symptoms instead of finding verified underlying causes; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:16.290
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
